{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a delivery sends events: a plain sink that records the batches it receives."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns. Batches that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return promptly and honour cancellation: a delivery waits for it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is cancelled. A destination handles its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"title":"Destination","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Destination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L23"}},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Destinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"],"title":"Conforming Types","kind":"relationships","type":"conformingTypes"}],"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/InMemoryDestination":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","url":"\/documentation\/destinations\/inmemorydestination","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that keeps the newest records it receives, in memory, for the app to read."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/Destination/accepting(_:)":